WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Hello, I'm Tanja, a specialist, certified nutritionist-dietitian,

2
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.940
master of public health, hypnotherapist and psychotherapist under supervision.

3
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.040
Today we're talking about nutrition for Hashimoto's disease.

4
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:28.720
Hello, Hashimoto's is an autoimmune disease.

5
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.080
It can be treated with medication, and you can also manage without medication,

6
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.520
it's just not the topic we'll talk about today.

7
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:43.660
Everything related to that must be agreed with your endocrinologist.

8
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:53.580
In any case it's very important to monitor the situation, regularly measure TSH, FT3, FT4, and also antibodies.

9
00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:05.520
At first only the antibodies are elevated, and, as I say, for the same reason, together with your endocrinologist you'll decide whether therapy is needed or not.

10
00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:18.520
In any case, what can help is changing your diet, if your current diet isn't the best, so we'll talk about that.

11
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:34.100
Besides, it's important to me that you know: along with Hashimoto's, polycystic ovary syndrome, insulin resistance often occur, and that the chances of obesity and other chronic diseases are higher.

12
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:42.520
That's why it's very important for us to act in time and change the lifestyle itself.

13
00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:50.480
I'll name five important things you need to know when it comes to nutrition for Hashimoto's.

14
00:01:51.460 --> 00:02:05.600
Then I'll give you recommendations on some supplements, which, of course, again need to be agreed with your endocrinologist,

15
00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:10.160
who knows your state of health, your therapy, your habits, etc.

16
00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:14.060
So treat what I say only as a general recommendation,

17
00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:19.060
which must always and in any case be adjusted to you.

18
00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:27.060
The first thing I want you to know is the story with gluten.

19
00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:35.060
In people with underactive thyroid, the chances of having celiac disease are higher too.

20
00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:40.060
That's an autoimmune disease too. Actually, it's a general rule.

21
00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:48.060
If we have one autoimmune disease, we are, unfortunately, prone to some others too.

22
00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:54.060
That's so. As for gluten, the chances of celiac disease are higher.

23
00:02:54.060 --> 00:03:05.060
But if you don't have celiac disease, that is, complete gluten intolerance, can gluten sensitivity exist? It can.

24
00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:15.320
We found an interesting study that confirmed that when people with Hashimoto's reduce gluten intake,

25
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:29.320
the antibodies that are regularly checked also decrease — we said this at the start — by which the condition is monitored, and vitamin D levels likewise rise.

26
00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:36.320
So, vitamin D is very important, it's one of the supplements recommended in a large number of cases.

27
00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:46.320
Where is gluten? It's in grains: first of all wheat, then rye, barley.

28
00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:58.320
Oats don't contain gluten, but because of the way they're grown they can often be contaminated with it, which isn't a big problem if you don't have celiac disease.

29
00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:25.620
If you only want to cut gluten down a little, exclude it because, as I said, it's beneficial for most people with Hashimoto's, then it's perfectly fine to eat oats and products labeled "may contain traces of gluten," because the main thing is to remove the main sources of gluten, above all wheat, whose gluten creates the most problems.

30
00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:40.680
So, that's it on gluten, and we move on to the second important thing I want you to know about nutrition for Hashimoto's — it's lactose, lactose intolerance.

31
00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:51.500
A study shows that around 75% of people with Hashimoto's have lactose intolerance at the same time.

32
00:04:51.500 --> 00:05:01.260
And that's one of the reasons why I often recommend to my clients to exclude cow's milk.

33
00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:08.880
Because a large number of my clients have either underactive thyroid or insulin resistance,

34
00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:17.720
and, as I say, one can drag the other along, so I simply like to prevent everything from the start so there are no problems later.

35
00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:31.720
But what I would advise you and what I do with my clients is the most effective, because you need to look at the whole picture and at what we want to achieve with nutrition.

36
00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:43.720
Very important for us is gut flora, microflora, the microbiome, that is, it's a completely new world in nutrition, so to speak,

37
00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:50.060
and actually our perhaps second brain is in the gut, if one can put it that way.

38
00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:57.120
In any case, fermented dairy products are very beneficial for this microbiome.

39
00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:05.160
For the same reason, although they contain lactose too, I advise keeping them in the diet.

40
00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:13.000
That is, kefir, yogurt, sour milk, sour cream — all this may be more beneficial

41
00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.240
than this lactose will interfere.

42
00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:27.220
But, on the other hand, I recommend excluding cow's milk, which, first, has more lactose, and second, this lactose is much harder to digest

43
00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.680
than the lactose in fermented dairy.

44
00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:37.660
The third point — a recommendation of an anti-inflammatory diet.

45
00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:41.700
What is that? Basically, nothing special,

46
00:06:41.700 --> 00:07:03.280
there are no strict rules here, the point is to eat as many vegetables and fruits as possible, as much omega-3 as possible; what is omega-3? It's found in fatty fish, in fatty sea fish, in seeds like chia, like flax, and in nuts,

47
00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:17.340
most of all in the most ordinary walnuts, you don't have to buy some, I don't know, macadamia, Brazil nut; Brazil nut is good because of selenium, but that's all.

48
00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:27.720
So, our most ordinary walnut is the best source of omega-3 when it comes to nuts.

49
00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:43.340
Besides, all homemade food: homemade eggs, homemade meat — and that's exactly the fourth tip: eat as much homemade food as possible, that is, as little food full of additives as possible.

50
00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:54.380
Additives are not necessarily bad, additives are what extended our lives, that is, they help food not spoil, keep longer.

51
00:07:54.380 --> 00:08:11.620
But it seems we've now gone to the other extreme, and, you know, there exists — it's literally regulated by law — a dose of additives safe for daily intake,

52
00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:22.120
and these are large doses. As a rule, we won't exceed this safe dose.

53
00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:32.600
However, when every day we eat a lot of food full of additives, the question arises how much that can affect our health.

54
00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:45.600
And when we have an autoimmune disease, we're much more sensitive, and I personally think that in such a case the safe dose should be lowered a bit more.

55
00:08:45.600 --> 00:09:02.600
That's why homemade food, whatever you have: homemade eggs, homemade fermented dairy, homemade meat — it doesn't matter what, beef, pork, chicken — if it's homemade, it's best for you.

56
00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:22.160
And number five: goitrogens. This is a popular topic today. I often see on social media, they say: broccoli, cauliflower and all this cruciferous stuff — absolutely not if you have thyroid problems, it'll wreak havoc, it'll kill you, I don't know what else.

57
00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:38.400
The truth is that goitrogens interfere, that we want to reduce them, but what matters here is food preparation, that is, heat treatment.

58
00:09:38.400 --> 00:10:08.180
And here we come again to one big misconception: that raw food is the highest thing everyone should strive for; and if we eat something cooked or, God forbid, meat, then we're bad, we're this and that, we have no moral standards, we know nothing, and they're enlightened, I don't know what. So drop all these trendy things.

59
00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:22.780
Your health is the most important, you have one life, and however selfish this may sound — it isn't selfish, I think — take care of yourself, and drop all these enlightenments and the rest.

60
00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:35.780
The point is that if you boil cauliflower, broccoli and other cruciferous vegetables, the goitrogen content drops greatly, and you can eat them without problems.

61
00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:47.780
That is, if you don't eat several kilos of raw cauliflower and broccoli every day, it's perfectly fine to eat them the way I said, and they won't harm you.

62
00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:57.460
On the contrary, this fiber will help you both for the microbiome and for satiety and for insulin control.

63
00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:02.220
That's why I say: we can never look at things from one side.

64
00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:15.800
You need to take in the whole picture, because for any advice, any product, anything I tell you, someone can turn up and say: aha, you know, but that's bad because of this and that.

65
00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:35.300
Yes, for anything you can find a reason why it's bad, but if there are many more reasons why it's good, you need to know both sides of the story and weigh which is more — benefit or harm.

66
00:11:35.300 --> 00:12:04.060
As for supplements, I'll just list what's usually prescribed, but I'll repeat: this really needs to be discussed with an endocrinologist; even for my clients I don't intervene much here, it's not my specialty, supplements are something I studied from experience, but I'm not a pharmacist,

67
00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:08.060
and I simply don't intervene in what I don't know 100% from all sides.

68
00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:12.060
What's recommended, I said, is vitamin D,

69
00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:19.060
and it's, I'd venture to say, nearly safe to take on your own too.

70
00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:25.060
At any rate, today in any lab you can check your vitamin D level,

71
00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:30.060
it's a thousand-something dinars, and sometimes there are coupons too, so get a coupon to save,

72
00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:36.060
and then you can start taking vitamin D.

73
00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:45.060
What else is often prescribed is the already mentioned selenium, iron, zinc, magnesium.

74
00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:50.060
Sorry for my voice, this cold has been holding me for a long time.

75
00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:56.060
And one spice that can help with that anti-inflammatory diet,

76
00:12:56.060 --> 00:13:03.060
as we said — reducing all these inflammations in the body, which are often many in an autoimmune disease.

77
00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:11.060
It's turmeric, or rather curcumin from turmeric is very effective in this,

78
00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:19.060
so here's a recommendation: season your dishes with turmeric, it may be beneficial.

79
00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:30.500
So, to sum up: when we talk about nutrition, it's important to eat as many vegetables and fruits as possible, fresh as well as cooked,

80
00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:40.000
that is, you need to watch everything: fatty sea fish, eggs, homemade meat, fermented dairy products,

81
00:13:40.000 --> 00:14:03.280
nuts, seeds, olive oil, avocado, nut butters, that is, simply to get as many nutrients as possible from food itself and not resort to supplements so often, because here again it's a question of these additional substances, a question of how much of them gets absorbed,

82
00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:06.320
a question of money in the end,

83
00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:11.100
so what can be obtained through food is always the first recommendation.

84
00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:16.540
And two more very important things — lifestyle,

85
00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:23.700
for you to watch, as much as you can, your stress, that is, control stress better; go to therapy, it's really very helpful.

86
00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:31.760
If you go to therapy, it doesn't mean something is wrong with you; I really think everyone, everyone, everyone should go to therapy,

87
00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:42.360
find a therapist who suits you, and you'll see: it will help you on so many fronts of life.

88
00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:54.000
And last — rest, good sleep: sleep at night, not during the day, sleep 8 hours, as much as you can,

89
00:14:54.000 --> 00:15:05.560
and go to bed a bit earlier; I really understand that we can't always do that, but when it comes to health, we simply must set our priorities.

90
00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:15.760
Well, that's all for this video. This is what you asked for, so I'm listening to you, keep suggesting topics, write in the comments.

91
00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:23.240
I'll try to answer as many of them as possible, the ones that are close to me, that I know, of course.

92
00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:39.880
In any case subscribe to the channel if you haven't yet, it's free, give the video a like if you liked it, as a sign of support,

93
00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:41.700
follow me on Instagram,

94
00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:53.060
and we'll keep meeting. Bye!